---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import Heading from "../../components/Heading.astro";
import Prose from "../../components/Prose.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About Me — João Silva | @odevjoao"
  description="Get to know me better."
>
  <script
    slot="head"
    type="application/ld+json"
    set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "AboutPage",
      name: "About Me — João Silva | @odevjoao",
      description: "Get to know me better.",
      url: new URL("/en/about", Astro.site).href,
      isPartOf: {
        "@type": "WebSite",
        name: "João Silva | @odevjoao",
        url: Astro.site?.href,
      },
    })}
  />
  <section class="about">
    <Heading as="h1">About Me</Heading>
    <Prose>
      <p>
        I was born in a city dubbed the Brazilian Switzerland in the interior of
        Rio de Janeiro, Brazil. Surrounded by lush greenery and beautiful
        landscapes, Benito di Paula was inspired there and wrote the song
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BDyxUQaG73E" target="_blank"
          >"Homem da Montanha"</a
        >. Besides being passionate about games and a huge fan of professional
        wrestling (WWE), I build software in JavaScript and TypeScript.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am currently a software engineer at
        <a href="https://ssparisi.software/" target="_blank">SS Parisi</a>.
        Working as a full-stack developer, I help implement and maintain
        accounting-sector systems that require high availability and throughput.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lately I have been discovering a new interest in Brazilian civic tech,
        building solutions that foster engagement, transparency, and social
        impact while improving the relationship between citizens and government.
        To support that, I started a Discord community called
        <a href="https://discord.gg/DNMrfEep" target="_blank"
          >🇧🇷 Civic Tech Brasil 🇧🇷</a
        > so it can be a gathering point for devs working on projects like these.
      </p>
      <p>
        As a creator, I launched this blog to discuss more technical matters. I
        also publish a weekly newsletter that feels more informal, sharing my
        study insights, summaries, tips, and projects—all grounded in my
        professional experience. The newsletter is called
        <a href="https://devdamontanha.substack.com" target="_blank"
          >"Dev da Montanha"</a
        >, a nod to the Benito di Paula song mentioned above.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm beginning my adventure as an author and plan to publish books and
        e-books soon.
      </p>
      <p>
        The internet gave me everything I have today. Being Gen Z, I practically
        grew up with it. I have the privilege of working as a programmer and
        intend to keep doing so for many years. I do not see myself being
        replaced by Artificial Intelligence; I will use it to become even more
        productive. I am certain that when we work on something we love with a
        purpose behind it, we never lose the motivation to keep working. My
        purpose in programming is to help people by solving their problems with
        well-planned software.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: var(--width-content);
  }
</style>
